4. Record the extracted xattrs again. Apply only the exact user-consent action
   in Â§4 when quarantine is present, record it and its exit status, and record
   the resulting binary xattr state.
5. Run exactly `./iolbox start`, with no asset, payload, machine, profile, or
   Lima override. Save the full output and exit status. This single command
   must create the default durable VM, provision the exact bundled payload,
   reach real HTTP readiness, and open the GUI.
6. Do not confuse liveness with readiness. Require launcher success, an HTTP
   status below 500 at `http://127.0.0.1:4001/`, a rendered GUI, active guest
