===== INSTALL TOP 45 =====
   1: # Installing iolbox
   2: 
   3: iolbox is a lightweight, Windows-native lab tool for Cisco IOL and VPCS: a
   4: Go supervisor with an embedded browser GUI drives a small Linux runtime
   5: (wherever it runs best on your machine) and you drive it all from a browser
   6: tab. **iolbox ships no Cisco software** â€” you supply your own IOL `.bin`/
   7: `.iol` image files and hold the appropriate licenses for them; see the
   8: "First steps" section below for how images get loaded in on each target.
   9: 
  10: The v0.5.2 release publishes six deployable artifacts (plus `capture-helper.exe`,
  11: a small standalone Wireshark-bridge helper, and `SHA256SUMS-ci.txt` â€” which
  12: covers only the CI-built artifacts; the VMware/OVA/QEMU disk-image artifacts
  13: in sections 1, 2, and 6 are built and attached by hand and aren't in it).
  14: Pick the row that matches your situation:
  15: 
  16: | Your situation | Artifact | Section |
  17: |---|---|---|
  18: | Windows desktop/laptop, want the simplest path | `iolbox-launcher-v0.5.2-windows.zip` | [QEMU disk (Windows launcher)](#6-qemu-disk-windows-bundled-launcher) |
  19: | Windows desktop already running VMware Workstation/Player, or ESXi/VirtualBox | `iolbox-appliance-v0.5.2.ova` | [OVA](#1-ova-vmware-workstationplayer-esxi-virtualbox) |
  20: | Windows with WSL2/Hyper-V already enabled | `iolbox-rootfs.tar` | [WSL rootfs](#3-wsl-rootfs-wsl2) |
  21: | Proxmox homelab | `iolbox-ct-v0.5.2.tar.zst` | [Proxmox LXC](#4-proxmox-lxc) |
  22: | Existing Linux server / cloud VM / on-prem hypervisor guest | `iolbox-server-v0.5.2.tar.gz` | [Native (systemd)](#5-native-systemd-linux-server) |
  23: 
  24: All six run the identical Go supervisor and (except the native target's
  25: build) the identical Debian-slim runtime â€” see `runtime/README.md`'s "one
  26: rootfs, two packages" note. Whichever you pick, the GUI ends up at
  27: **`http://<host>:4001`**, and it has **no login of any kind**. Only expose
  28: it on localhost or a network you trust (see the security note repeated in
  29: each section).
  30: 
  31: Default sizing for every target is **4 vCPUs / 4096 MB RAM** (source:
  32: `runtime/resources.env`, `IOLBOX_VCPUS=4` / `IOLBOX_RAM_MB=4096`); each
  33: section below notes where to change it for that target.
  34: 
  35: A Docker image also exists as a seventh, build-from-source option if you'd
  36: rather not touch WSL2/Hyper-V/VMware at all â€” see `docker/README.md`. It
  37: isn't one of the six release artifacts and isn't covered in depth here.
  38: 
  39: ---
  40: 
  41: ## 1. OVA (VMware Workstation/Player, ESXi, VirtualBox)
  42: 
  43: **Artifact:** `iolbox-appliance-v0.5.2.ova`
  44: **Source:** `runtime/pack-ova.sh`, `runtime/REDEPLOY.md`
  45: 
