 444: ## Apple Silicon macOS (Lima)
 445: 
 446: The macOS launcher provisions an arm64 Linux guest and runs the x86_64
 447: supervisor/IOL payload through Lima Rosetta. A qualified Apple Silicon guest
 448: omits `i386` from `hello.features`; the GUI keeps ELF32 images visible for
 449: inventory but disables their palette, picker, replacement, and start controls
 450: with the measured capability reason. x86_64 IOL images remain supported. The
 451: supervisor's `arch` field describes the guest/runtime, not the IOL ELF.
 452: 
 453: `iolbox-launcher diagnose` reports measured `guest_arch`, `execution`,
 454: `guest_kernel`, `canary_verdict`, `service`, `http`, `hello`, and
 455: `capability_policy` predicates. Values read from the host structural file are
 456: labelled `last attested`; they are not live guest measurements.
